{"page":425,"verses":[{"verse_key":"33:51","surah":33,"ayah":51,"ar_uthmani":"۞ تُرْجِى مَن تَشَآءُ مِنْهُنَّ وَتُـْٔوِىٓ إِلَيْكَ مَن تَشَآءُ ۖ وَمَنِ ٱبْتَغَيْتَ مِمَّنْ عَزَلْتَ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكَ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ أَدْنَىٰٓ أَن تَقَرَّ أَعْيُنُهُنَّ وَلَا يَحْزَنَّ وَيَرْضَيْنَ بِمَآ ءَاتَيْتَهُنَّ كُلُّهُنَّ ۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى قُلُوبِكُمْ ۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَلِيمًا حَلِيمًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"You may make any of [your women] wait and receive any of them as you wish, but you will not be at fault if you invite one whose turn you have previously set aside: this way it is more likely that they will be satisfied and will not be distressed and will all be content with what you have given them. God knows what is in your hearts: God is all knowing, forbearing.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"۞ تُرْجِى","en_gloss":"You may defer","transliteration":"tur'jī","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":2,"ar":"مَن","en_gloss":"whom","transliteration":"man","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":3,"ar":"تَشَآءُ","en_gloss":"you will","transliteration":"tashāu","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":4,"ar":"مِنْهُنَّ","en_gloss":"of them","transliteration":"min'hunna","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":5,"ar":"وَتُـْٔوِىٓ","en_gloss":"or you may take","transliteration":"watu'wī","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":6,"ar":"إِلَيْكَ","en_gloss":"to yourself","transliteration":"ilayka","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":7,"ar":"مَن","en_gloss":"whom","transliteration":"man","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":8,"ar":"تَشَآءُ ۖ","en_gloss":"you will","transliteration":"tashāu","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":9,"ar":"وَمَنِ","en_gloss":"And whoever","transliteration":"wamani","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":10,"ar":"ٱبْتَغَيْتَ","en_gloss":"you desire","transliteration":"ib'taghayta","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":11,"ar":"مِمَّنْ","en_gloss":"of those whom","transliteration":"mimman","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":12,"ar":"عَزَلْتَ","en_gloss":"you (had) set aside ","transliteration":"ʿazalta","verse_key":"33:51"},{"pos":13,"ar":"فَلَا","en_glo