ِيمًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Believers, do not enter the Prophet’s apartments for a meal unless you are given permission to do so; do not linger until [a meal] is ready. When you are invited, go in; then, when you have taken your meal, leave. Do not stay on and talk, for that would offend the Prophet, though he would shrink from asking you to leave. God does not shrink from the truth. When you ask his wives for something, do so from behind a screen: this is purer both for your hearts and for theirs. It is not right for you to offend God’s Messenger, just as you should never marry his wives after him: that would be grievous in God’s eyes.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا","en_gloss":"O you who believe","transliteration":"yāayyuhā","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"O you who believe","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ءَامَنُوا۟","en_gloss":"O you who believe","transliteration":"āmanū","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":4,"ar":"لَا","en_gloss":"(Do) not","transliteration":"lā","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":5,"ar":"تَدْخُلُوا۟","en_gloss":"enter","transliteration":"tadkhulū","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":6,"ar":"بُيُوتَ","en_gloss":"(the) houses","transliteration":"buyūta","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":7,"ar":"ٱلنَّبِىِّ","en_gloss":"(of) the Prophet","transliteration":"l-nabiyi","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":8,"ar":"إِلَّآ","en_gloss":"except","transliteration":"illā","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":9,"ar":"أَن","en_gloss":"when","transliteration":"an","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":10,"ar":"يُؤْذَنَ","en_gloss":"permission is given","transliteration":"yu'dhana","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":11,"ar":"لَكُمْ","en_gloss":"to you","transliteration":"lakum","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":12,"ar":"إِلَىٰ","en_gloss":"for","transliteration":"ilā","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":13,"ar":"طَعَامٍ","en_gloss":"a meal","transliteration":"ṭaʿāmin","verse_key":"33:53"},{"pos":14,"ar":"غَيْرَ","en_gloss":"without","transliteration":"ghayra","